# Discord Layer

## Embed rules (discord.js v12)

```javascript
// ❌ BAD — Discord API 400: embed.description required
new MessageEmbed().setTitle("Team Info")

// ✅ GOOD
new MessageEmbed().setTitle("Team Info").setDescription("…")
```

Use base embeds from `HtbEmbeds`: `TARGET_INFO_BASE`, `TEAM_INFO_BASE`, `ERROR_BASE`, etc.

## Empty data guards

When cache is empty, return helpful embeds (not crash):

```javascript
// views/embeds.js pattern
if (!this.ds.TEAM_STATS?.name) {
  return this.ERROR_BASE
    .setTitle("Team data unavailable")
    .setDescription("HTB team data is not loaded yet. Try `seven force update`…")
}
```

## Message flow

1. `handleMessage()` → `understand()` (DialogFlow) or `resolveEnt()` (direct entity)
2. Intent handler in `bot.js` switch → `EGI.method()` → `SEND.embed()` or `SEND.human()`
3. `Send.embed()` handles typing delay, pickle mode, passthru

## resolveEnt()

Central entity resolver in `SevenDatastore`. Always pass `discordMessage` for self-reference ("i", "me"). Guard nested lookups when `MISC.FORTRESSES` etc. may be `{}`.

## Adding a feature

1. DialogFlow intent (or extend `resolveEnt` for direct queries)
2. Handler case in `bot.js`
3. Embed method in `HtbEmbeds` (views/embeds.js)
4. If new entity type: update `helpers/dflow.js` entity sync + `helpers/classes.js`

## Admin commands

- `forceUpdate` → `refresh({ force: true })` — smart team sync
- `admin_clearCached` → `refresh({ full: true })` — full re-fetch
